<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<definitions xmlns="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" id="defs_P_15_3" targetNamespace="http://tim-method.example/utility-wam/1.0" exporter="Utility WAM Industry Process Reference" exporterVersion="2026-08-28">
  <process id="P_15_3" name="15.3 Meet reporting and retention obligations" isExecutable="false">
    <documentation>All three processes are drawn. 15.3.2 branches on commodity and the branch is the substance of the group: 49 CFR 192.1007(e) and (g) with 191.11 make gas distribution integrity performance a FEDERAL filing, while IEEE 1366 supplies an electric distribution reliability METHOD that no federal rule requires anyone to file. Drawing one path over both would put a mandate on the electric side that does not exist, which is the same asymmetry 16 U.S.C. 824o creates everywhere else in this reference.

15.3.3 is retention and it is drawn with the hold as a gate rather than a note. 18 CFR 125.3 holds continuing plant inventory records for 25 years and specified work and authorisation records for 5 after the plant account clears; 49 CFR 192.709(a) is service-life retention for TRANSMISSION pipe, with (b) and (c) carrying the shorter periods. A record whose longest applicable obligation has not been established cannot be disposed of, and the gate says so.</documentation>
    <laneSet id="P_15_3_lanes">
      <lane id="l_153_comp" name="Compliance reporting">
        <flowNodeRef>n_153_t</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_153_coll</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_153_pop</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_153_app</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_153_sub</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_153_ack</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_153_e1</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_153_rt</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_153_meth</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_153_gas</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_153_el</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_153_class</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_153_iss</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_153_e2</flowNodeRef>
      </lane>
      <lane id="l_153_rec" name="Records management">
        <flowNodeRef>n_153_r</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_153_cls</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_153_bind</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_153_hold</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_153_keep</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_153_disp</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_153_e3</flowNodeRef>
      </lane>
    </laneSet>
    <startEvent id="n_153_t" name="Filing period or deadline opens"><timerEventDefinition id="n_153_t_td"/></startEvent>
    <serviceTask id="n_153_coll" name="Collect records and declarations"><documentation>15.3.1.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <userTask id="n_153_pop" name="Reconcile the population and resolve exceptions"><documentation>15.3.1. A reportable exception found here is a filing in its own right, not a footnote to this one.</documentation></userTask>
    <userTask id="n_153_app" name="Approve the submission"><documentation>15.3.1.</documentation></userTask>
    <sendTask id="n_153_sub" name="Submit on the required route"><documentation>15.3.1. For gas distribution integrity, the federal route under 49 CFR 192.1007(e) and (g).</documentation></sendTask>
    <receiveTask id="n_153_ack" name="Retain submission, acknowledgement and evidence"><documentation>15.3.1. The acknowledgement is part of the record; a submission with no acknowledgement retained is a claim that something was filed.</documentation></receiveTask>
    <endEvent id="n_153_e1" name="Obligation met"/>
    <startEvent id="n_153_rt" name="Reliability or safety period closes"><timerEventDefinition id="n_153_rt_td"/></startEvent>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_153_meth" name="Commodity and method"/>
    <serviceTask id="n_153_gas" name="Compile gas distribution integrity performance"><documentation>15.3.2. 49 CFR 192.1007(e) and (g) and 191.11. A federal duty, on a federal form.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_153_el" name="Calculate electric reliability on the IEEE 1366 method"><documentation>15.3.2. Including the major-event day treatment. IEEE 1366 is a method and not a federal filing mandate; whether it is filed at all is the State's rule.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <userTask id="n_153_class" name="Classify events and reconcile the population"><documentation>15.3.2. Event classification decides the number more than the arithmetic does, which is why 9.0 records interruptions the way it does.</documentation></userTask>
    <sendTask id="n_153_iss" name="Issue the report and retain its support"><documentation>15.3.2.</documentation></sendTask>
    <endEvent id="n_153_e2" name="Reliability or safety report issued"/>
    <startEvent id="n_153_r" name="A record requiring retention is produced"><messageEventDefinition id="n_153_r_md"/></startEvent>
    <serviceTask id="n_153_cls" name="Classify the record and its governing obligation"><documentation>15.3.3. 18 CFR 125.3 and 49 CFR 192.709 reach different record sets; the classification is what decides which.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_153_bind" name="Bind it to its work, asset and reporting context"><documentation>15.3.3. An unbound record satisfies a retention period and answers no question.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_153_hold" name="Hold or longer obligation in force"/>
    <endEvent id="n_153_keep" name="Retained under hold or the longer obligation"><documentation>15.3.3.</documentation></endEvent>
    <userTask id="n_153_disp" name="Dispose under authority at the end of the period"><documentation>15.3.3.</documentation></userTask>
    <endEvent id="n_153_e3" name="Disposition complete"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_153_t_n_153_coll" sourceRef="n_153_t" targetRef="n_153_coll" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_153_coll_n_153_pop" sourceRef="n_153_coll" targetRef="n_153_pop" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_153_pop_n_153_app" sourceRef="n_153_pop" targetRef="n_153_app" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_153_app_n_153_sub" sourceRef="n_153_app" targetRef="n_153_sub" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_153_sub_n_153_ack" sourceRef="n_153_sub" targetRef="n_153_ack" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_153_ack_n_153_e1" sourceRef="n_153_ack" targetRef="n_153_e1" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_153_rt_n_153_meth" sourceRef="n_153_rt" targetRef="n_153_meth" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_153_meth_n_153_gas" sourceRef="n_153_meth" targetRef="n_153_gas" name="gas distribution"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[commodity = "gas"]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_153_meth_n_153_el" sourceRef="n_153_meth" targetRef="n_153_el" name="electric distribution"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[commodity = "electric"]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_153_gas_n_153_class" sourceRef="n_153_gas" targetRef="n_153_class" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_153_el_n_153_class" sourceRef="n_153_el" targetRef="n_153_class" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_153_class_n_153_iss" sourceRef="n_153_class" targetRef="n_153_iss" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_153_iss_n_153_e2" sourceRef="n_153_iss" targetRef="n_153_e2" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_153_r_n_153_cls" sourceRef="n_153_r" targetRef="n_153_cls" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_153_cls_n_153_bind" sourceRef="n_153_cls" targetRef="n_153_bind" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_153_bind_n_153_hold" sourceRef="n_153_bind" targetRef="n_153_hold" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_153_hold_n_153_keep" sourceRef="n_153_hold" targetRef="n_153_keep" name="hold in force"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[holdInForce = true]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_153_hold_n_153_disp" sourceRef="n_153_hold" targetRef="n_153_disp" name="period ended, no hold"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_153_disp_n_153_e3" sourceRef="n_153_disp" targetRef="n_153_e3" name=""/>
  </process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="dg_P_15_3">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="pl_P_15_3" bpmnElement="P_15_3">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="sh_n_153_t" bpmnElement="n_153_t"><dc:Bounds x="132" y="217" width="36" height="36"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
